1
00:00:13,650 --> 00:00:15,930
Excuse me. Is this seat taken?

2
00:00:15,930 --> 00:00:17,420
No, it's not taken.

3
00:00:17,420 --> 00:00:18,570
Oh, thank you.

4
00:00:18,570 --> 00:00:20,120
Oh, let me help you with this.

5
00:00:20,120 --> 00:00:26,670
Oh, thank you.

6
00:00:26,670 --> 00:00:27,850
Do you want to sit by the window?

7
00:00:27,850 --> 00:00:30,780
No, no, no. I like the aisle seat better.

8
00:00:30,780 --> 00:00:39,410
Please, you sit by the window.

9
00:00:39,410 --> 00:00:41,450
My name is Stewart... Malcolm Stewart.

10
00:00:41,450 --> 00:00:42,450
Pleased to meet you.

11
00:00:42,450 --> 00:00:50,660
I'm Elsa Tobin. How do you do?

12
00:00:50,660 --> 00:00:52,700
Do you live in New York?

13
00:00:52,700 --> 00:00:55,160
No, no. I'm from Florida.

14
00:00:55,160 --> 00:01:00,280
I am, too. But didn't you just get on?

15
00:01:00,280 --> 00:01:02,790
No, no. I just changed my seat.

16
00:01:02,790 --> 00:01:04,760
A man next to me was smoking,

17
00:01:04,760 --> 00:01:10,480
and smoke really bothers me.

18
00:01:10,480 --> 00:01:12,490
Where are you from in Florida?

19
00:01:12,490 --> 00:01:15,110
Titusville. It's near Orlando.

20
00:01:15,110 --> 00:01:17,410
Small world. I'm from Titusville, too.

21
00:01:17,410 --> 00:01:21,340
Really? What part?

22
00:01:21,340 --> 00:01:24,180
My husband and I live near Spaceport.

23
00:01:24,180 --> 00:01:26,740
I know that area.

24
00:01:26,740 --> 00:01:31,880
My house is only a few miles from Spaceport.

25
00:01:31,880 --> 00:01:32,960
Do you still live there?

26
00:01:32,960 --> 00:01:35,460
Oh yes, yes. My husband's there now.

27
00:01:35,460 --> 00:01:41,700
He couldn't take time off to come to New York with me.

28
00:01:41,700 --> 00:01:43,590
Do you still live there?

29
00:01:43,590 --> 00:01:49,740
No. I sold the house and the furniture,

30
00:01:49,740 --> 00:01:53,940
put a few personal things in an old trunk,

31
00:01:53,940 --> 00:01:56,800
and shipped it to my children in New York.

32
00:01:56,800 --> 00:01:58,970
That's my destination.

33
00:01:58,970 --> 00:02:00,740
Are you married?

34
00:02:00,740 --> 00:02:04,720
My wife died four years ago.

35
00:02:04,720 --> 00:02:08,820
She was a wonderful woman. A real friend.

36
00:02:08,820 --> 00:02:14,070
I'm sorry. Really, I'm sorry.

37
00:02:14,070 --> 00:02:17,110
Lots of wonderful memories.

38
00:02:17,110 --> 00:02:19,180
We were married almost fifty years.

39
00:02:19,180 --> 00:02:22,040
Well, forty-seven, to be exact.

40
00:02:22,040 --> 00:02:25,350
John and I celebrate our fortieth anniversary next month.

41
00:02:25,350 --> 00:02:30,870
Oh, congratulations! That's nice.

42
00:02:30,870 --> 00:02:32,630
What does John do?

43
00:02:32,630 --> 00:02:34,740
He's an aerospace engineer

44
00:02:34,740 --> 00:02:38,090
and works for Orlando Aircraft Corporation.

45
00:02:38,090 --> 00:02:42,950
He started with them almost forty years ago.

46
00:02:42,950 --> 00:02:45,020
What do you do?

47
00:02:45,020 --> 00:02:49,950
I just retired. Had my own company.

48
00:02:49,950 --> 00:02:56,690
A construction company. Roads, bridges, big stuff.

49
00:02:56,690 --> 00:03:04,210
But I just sold it and retired.

50
00:03:04,210 --> 00:03:09,730
Excuse me, ma'am. Ticket, please.

51
00:03:09,730 --> 00:03:13,630
Would you kindly hold these keys, please?

52
00:03:13,630 --> 00:03:16,170
I have a ticket, I know.

53
00:03:16,170 --> 00:03:18,060
I was in the smoking section.

54
00:03:18,060 --> 00:03:21,340
It's OK, lady. Take your time.

55
00:03:21,340 --> 00:03:24,090
I'm sure it's in your purse, Mrs.Tobin.

56
00:03:24,090 --> 00:03:29,500
Oh, here it is.

57
00:03:29,500 --> 00:03:31,650
And here are your keys.

58
00:03:31,650 --> 00:03:38,350
Thank you.

59
00:03:38,350 --> 00:03:40,460
Do you have family in New York?

60
00:03:40,460 --> 00:03:46,190
No, no. But I do have very close friends in New York City.

61
00:03:46,190 --> 00:03:49,490
We like to go to the theater together.

62
00:03:49,490 --> 00:03:51,110
You said you have family in New York.

63
00:03:51,110 --> 00:03:53,200
Yes, indeed.

64
00:03:53,200 --> 00:03:57,200
A son and his wife and their three children-

65
00:03:57,200 --> 00:03:58,530
my grandchildren.

66
00:03:58,530 --> 00:03:59,670
You must be excited.

67
00:03:59,670 --> 00:04:04,080
I can't wait, to see them!

68
00:04:04,080 --> 00:04:05,510
Are you going to live with them?

69
00:04:05,510 --> 00:04:06,300
Yes.

70
00:04:06,300 --> 00:04:08,350
Permanently?

71
00:04:08,350 --> 00:04:12,380
Well... they want me to,

72
00:04:12,380 --> 00:04:14,890
but it's too early to know for sure.

73
00:04:14,890 --> 00:04:17,590
I'm pretty independent.

74
00:04:17,590 --> 00:04:22,480
I tried to teach my kids the importance of independence,

75
00:04:22,480 --> 00:04:27,920
but I'm not sure I want to be alone.

76
00:04:27,920 --> 00:04:33,020
Some people don't mind being alone. I do.

77
00:04:33,020 --> 00:04:37,030
I understand. But tell me.

78
00:04:37,030 --> 00:04:39,990
Why did you stop working?

79
00:04:39,990 --> 00:04:48,660
I retired because... I wanted to be with my family.

80
00:04:48,660 --> 00:04:51,660
I didn't want to be alone anymore!
